{
  "id": "navigation/constructor_calls/01_initializers",
  "topic": "navigation",
  "subtopic": "constructor_calls",
  "title": "Initializer lists",
  "summary": "A delegating or base initializer's name leads to the constructor it calls",
  "prose": "Go-to-definition, declaration, hover, highlights and references on the\nclass name of `Widget() : Widget(1, 2)` or `: Base(size)` answer the constructor\nthe initializer calls; go-to-type-definition answers the class. Its\nparenthesis still leads to the constructor, without counting as a second\nreference.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clice#1152"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "struct Base {\n    Base(int x);\n};\n\nstruct Widget : Base {\n    Widget(int width, int height);\n    Widget(int size) : Base(size) {}\n    Widget() : Widget(1, 2) {}\n};\n",
